        "description": "The source grade demineralized water is explicitly named in all nine admitted ingredient1448 rows across DSMZ1191,1279,1600 and1793, including the source abbreviations H2O demin. and Aqua dem. It is represented as a distinct preparation-qualified solvent, with CHEBI15377 water as a broader molecular parent only. No ion-removal method, conductivity, resistivity, reagent standard, quantitative purity or universal sterility is asserted. The one sterile addition in DSMZ1600 retains that operational qualifier in its recipe; this owner does not globally equate sterile water, distilled water or tap water. The exact-name OLS search found TransformON c_ROHSUO, but TFO is outside the maintained OntologySourceEnum and its conductivity scope is not specified by these sources; the candidate is preserved as context rather than silently adopted or reported absent.",
