        "description": "TOGO M491 provides the explicit prepared basal grouping and preparation comment. Its original JCM490 endpoint capture says Nothing found; no successful original formulation inspection is claimed. TOGO groups phosphate salts with this base, unlike M481; the provider-defined version is preserved without declaring equality to JCM480. Source transcription basis (literal input amounts, not calculated stock concentrations): distilled water: 900 ml; MgSO4・7H2O: 0.5 g; Yeast extract: 0.5 g; NaCl: 2.25 g; CaCl2・2H2O: 0.25 g; KH2PO4: 0.227 g; NH4Cl: 0.5 g; K2HPO4: 0.348 g; Resazurin: 1 mg; Casitone (BD-Difco): 0.5 g; Trace vitamins (see Medium [M190]): 10 ml; Trace element solution (see Medium No. [480]): 1 ml; Se/W solution (see Medium [M312]): 1 ml. No batch-to-final-volume conversion is made. Handling atmosphere is not listed as a material part; pH reagents are source inputs, without an assertion of unchanged molecular species after pH adjustment. Nested formulations remain source-qualified named parts where exact composition/owner identity is not established.",
