        "description": "M2241 DH micronutrient solution explicitly uses0.5mLconcentrated H2SO4. Source names a concentrated preparation but supplies no numerical assay, water amount or density. Represent only this source-qualified material; no97%,98% or standard molarity is invented. TOGO M1020/JCM970 specifies2mLconcentrated sulfuric acid; ATCC920-derived M3142/M3140 micronutrient stocks specify0.5mL. This bounded named-material record captures only the shared stated concentrated-acid description; no equal assay or full-formulation equivalence is claimed between the source preparations. ATCC203/TOGO M2236 SolutionC lists0.05mLconcentrated H2SO4 alongside0.5gFeSO4·7H2O,0.14gEDTA and100mLwater. Those other constituents belong to SolutionC, not the supplied concentrated acid. Assay and solvent composition of the acid are unspecified. UTEX BBM trace stock explicitly lists10mLconcentrated H2SO4 and makes the total trace-stock volume1L. That establishes the acid volume per litre of trace stock, not the acid assay. This owner captures the supplied concentrated acid with no assumed97/98% strength. Source IDs do not establish distinct substances, so one bounded unspecified-assay material is proposed. This shared record asserts only the common named preparation, not equal commercial assay or interchangeability of unknown formulations. Component completeness is UNKNOWN. Unstated solvent, hydration, assay and final volume are not invented. This is the named preparation at the cited source scope; no full-formulation equivalence with other products is asserted.",
