        "description": "Polyoxyethylene sorbitan mono-oleate explicitly identified as Tween80 is polysorbate80 CHEBI:53426. The polyoxyethylene qualifier distinguishes it from sorbitan monooleate; this is a safe source alias to the existing Tween80 owner, not to Span80. Final-review correction: #1226: evidence[1] MANUAL_CURATION→LLM_SUGGESTION; actual LLM authorship, not scientific approval. CH-07: The retained InChI and SMILES exactly reproduce ChEBI:53426 representative annotations. ChEBI also defines a polymer with w+x+y+z=20 and supplies a variable polymer formula. These strings are representative database structures, not a measurement that commercial Tween80 is a single discrete C32H60O10 species; the existing variable formula and supported polyoxyethylene/Tween80 source alias are retained.",
