        "description": "Folic acid with vitaminB9 is an explicit single solute even where nested in a vitamin stock. CHEBI:27470 identifies folic acid and supports the B9 label. Add the qualified alias to the existing owner while retaining the original nested occurrence context. Final-review correction: #1226: evidence[2] MANUAL_CURATION→LLM_SUGGESTION; actual LLM authorship, not scientific approval. CH-01: synonyms[7] 'Folinic acid (citrovorum)': reject_resolving_identity_preserve_text_and_source. Folinic acid is5-formyltetrahydrofolic acid15640 with distinct formula from folic acid27470; JCM537 lists folinic and folic components separately. CH-06: synonyms[23] 'Folic acid (5 μg/μL)': reject_resolving_identity_preserve_text_and_source. NBRC1604 uses10µl of5µg/µl folic-acid stock; this is an aliquoted preparation, not the neat folic-acid identity.",
