        ],
        "description": "The raw source(NH4)6Mo7O24 x4H2O, ingredient120 CAS12054-85-2 and mass1235.86 identify hexaammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate86244. Diammonium orthomolybdate91249 has one Mo and two ammoniums and is not its parent. The current wrong owner already rejects the tetrahydrate strings but still resolves the anhydrous heptamolybdate formula; reject that residual polyanion alias and link the source to the existing correct tetrahydrate owner. OLS86244's prose says heptahydrate in error; its name/formula/mass and source CAS all specify four waters. Final-review correction: #1226: evidence[4] MANUAL_CURATION→LLM_SUGGESTION; actual LLM authorship, not scientific approval. CH-05: individually assess seven listed malformed molybdate aliases; preserve demonstrated TOGO M412/JCM414 damaged-label RAW_TEXT and reject unresolved/incompatible formula tokens. Original text/source and history retained. CH-05: synonyms[1] '(NH4)6Mo7O4': reject_resolving_identity_preserve_text_and_source. The literal formula has only O4 and omits hydrate water; no exact original-source correction for this whole global token was established. CH-05: synonyms[3] '(NH4)6MoO24·4H2O': reject_resolving_identity_preserve_text_and_source. TOGO1032/941 and original JCM979/900 repeat the missing-Mo-count formula; the source does not independently restore seven molybdenums. CH-05: synonyms[4] '(NH4)6MoO7O24': reject_resolving_identity_preserve_text_and_source. The repeated-O malformed formula omits hydrate water; neither charge-balanced heptamolybdate nor four-water identity is literally established. CH-05: synonyms[5] '(NH4)6MoO7O24 x 4 H2O': reject_resolving_identity_preserve_text_and_source. TOGO2346 links DSMZ600, whose Hutner salts explicitly reference DSMZ590; original DSMZ590 repeats the malformed MoO7O24 formula. This chain does not correct its oxygen/molybdenum notation. CH-05: synonyms[7] '(NH4)MoO7O24': reject_resolving_identity_preserve_text_and_source. This literal token omits five ammoniums, has repeated oxygen notation and no hydrate water; its complete four-water identity is not established. CH-05: synonyms[8] '(NH4)MoO7O24 x 4 H2O': reject_resolving_identity_preserve_text_and_source. Original DSMZ1144 repeats the malformed one-ammonium/repeated-O formula; a neighboring Hutner recipe is not a source correction. CH-05: synonyms[6] '(NH4)Mo7O24·4H2O': retain_proven_damaged_source_RAW_TEXT_with_occurrence_scope. Exact TOGO M412 source metadata links JCM414. TOGO drops the ammonium subscript6 at the0.5g trace-stock component; original JCM414 prints (NH4)6Mo7O24·4H2O. Retain this existing RAW_TEXT under the documented damaged-label carve-out, not as a new exact formula or blanket correction of other occurrences. M944 also links original JCM903 with the correct six-ammonium formula. M1196 links JCM1118, which itself repeats the missing-six formula; that occurrence remains unresolved and is not released by these two verified typo bridges.",
