        ],
        "description": "NBRC943 explicitly specifies (NH4)6Mo7O24·2H2O9.25mg in modified Hutner solution. Formula is chemically coherent and no competing primary recipe formula was found. Exact tetrahydrate term86244 is not an identity match; its own prose says heptahydrate despite four-water formula, so formula/structure take precedence. Preserve a distinct source-stated two-water registry identity without replacing its waters. No exact ontology term or CAS is asserted; registry identity preserves the stated formula. Final-review correction: #1226: evidence[0] MANUAL_CURATION→LLM_SUGGESTION; actual LLM authorship, not scientific approval. CH-10 qualification: retain this distinct source-stated local hydrate identity and exact formal water count under §3. No measured crystal phase, supplier purity, new CAS or molecular mass is asserted. This does not release the separate source1201/#344/#896 owner conflict. Bounded live heptamolybdate and ammonium-molybdate searches found tetrahydrate86244 and orthomolybdate91249, neither a parent identity for this dihydrate. General ammonium-salt47704 and hydrate35505 are broad, non-equivalent class anchors; no closer heptamolybdate parent was established in those searches. Retain the verified hydrate35505 asymmetric class mapping rather than substitute the chemically wrong orthomolybdate or invent an exact term. Parent specificity is a recorded limitation, not a physical-phase gate.",
