        "description": "Re-read the complete acid owner history: June16 research-based merge treated alpha-ketoglutamate as alpha-ketoglutarate and then equated it with the acid. Even if typo correction is accepted, CHEBI16810 defines the dianion whereas30915 is the acid; the history is not source2384 procurement proof. Propose changing the ambiguous global alias to rejected provenance while retaining the historical merge event and all role data. Final-review correction: CH-06: synonyms[6] 'alpha-ketoglutaric acid (100 mM).': reject_resolving_identity_preserve_text_and_source. TOGO2388 lists0.1ml of100mM alpha-ketoglutaric acid; the label specifies an aliquoted stock. Solvent is unstated and not invented; keep separate from pure30915.",
