        "description": "Method-only successor for W04-FINAL-001: actual current unique exactCAS lookup supports CAS_RN_LOOKUP; native provenance evidence and truthful history appended. Exact provenance binds MediaDive1188 to DSMZ1344 Taps 17.4 g. The original recipe and manufacturer T5130/108320 nomenclature establish the conventional TAPS buffer name, N-[tris(hydroxymethyl)methyl]-3-aminopropanesulfonic acid (CHEBI:191055, CAS29915-38-6). Represent that free-buffer identity separately from CAS91000-53-2 sodium salt and from the automatically matched Tyr-Arg-Phe-Sar peptide. No Sigma purchase, lot assay or sodium salt is inferred from pH8.3. The existing sodium-salt alias rejection remains valid. Specific supplier/catalogue/lot and measured supplied purity are unknown; these are not prerequisites for the conventional free-buffer identity proposal. Source metadata repair and whole-owner/export acceptance remain held.",
