      "complete_proposal": {
        "proposal_id": "FRV1-BIO-P-filtered_seawater",
        "case_ids": [
          "CM_NAME:12fab181fb7a8d829e375acb04a7267dabc69b22aa48ee624c3c417aee9e473d",
          "CM_NAME:7ce67d784e648c4b596c43e62c319bf29cdf19710f09454cde8be8612d650b98"
        ],
        "description": "Retain two supported filtration aliases and make two inherited insufficiently scoped aliases nonresolving, after actual source reconstruction. Final-review qualification of the historical #260 dilution rationale: the original CCAP PE footnote explicitly says to filter natural seawater, reduce it to 95% using glass distilled water, and autoclave. That prepared input is then dosed at 950 cm3; the prior dilution is not inferred from the receiving-medium dose. The literal 95%-strength label is retained as REJECTED_LABEL on this bare filtered-seawater owner, without inventing the percentage basis, final volume, component ratio or a new preparation owner. The unqualified Natural seawater alias is also nonresolving: its recovered JCM1377 contexts state natural seawater without filtration. Supported Filtered natural seawater and Natural seawater (filtrated) aliases remain. Earlier #260 mapping evidence and histories are preserved as historical rationale, superseded only on these alias applicability points by this source-backed qualification. The two assigned filtered cases are not reinterpreted as the 95% preparation. Sources: https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_PE.pdf ; https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1377 .",
        "evidence_ids": [
