        ],
        "description": "The source names a nominal 95% ethanol preparation. The percentage basis, solvent balance, denaturants and historical product specification are unreported. Different source accessions or receiving stocks prove neither equal nor different supplied preparations. A shared bounded nominal representation is a possible coordinator outcome; exact historical formulation equality and a final owner choice remain unresolved under #1237. This identifier is retained only as a conditional historical proposal handle. Do not install all four candidates as proven distinct substances. Retain all 17 precise occurrence routes and the original source lineages. CHEBI:16236 grounds the named ethanol component only; NCIT:C185110 is not approved because it specifically requires aqueous 95% by volume. No numerical component percentage, water balance or whole-stock molecular identity is inferred. All inherited holds remain. Source-specific context: ATCC 1490 defines the vitamin K1 receiving stock with 0.15 ml vitamin K1 and 30 ml of nominal 95% ethanol. ATCC 1703 and 1539 explicitly reuse that recipe, represented by TOGO M2576, M2574 and M2618. The three routed occurrences remain together. These receiving-stock quantities do not define the percentage basis or balance of the supplied ethanol.",
