        "description": "The source names a nominal 95% ethanol preparation. The percentage basis, solvent balance, denaturants and historical product specification are unreported. Different source accessions or receiving stocks prove neither equal nor different supplied preparations. A shared bounded nominal representation is a possible coordinator outcome; exact historical formulation equality and a final owner choice remain unresolved under #1237. This identifier is retained only as a conditional historical proposal handle. Do not install all four candidates as proven distinct substances. Retain all 17 precise occurrence routes and the original source lineages. CHEBI:16236 grounds the named ethanol component only; NCIT:C185110 is not approved because it specifically requires aqueous 95% by volume. No numerical component percentage, water balance or whole-stock molecular identity is inferred. All inherited holds remain. Source-specific context: ATCC 1257 ETSA, represented by TOGO M2568, lists 100 ml of nominal 95% ethanol in the hemin receiving stock and 50 ml in the menadione receiving stock. The separately added 100 ml and 50 ml water belong to those receiving stocks, not to the unidentified balance of the supplied ethanol. Preserve the one frozen occurrence and its two nested source uses; the flattened 150 g/L value is not a measured ethanol concentration.",
