      "condition_fields": {
        "description": "This source-qualified commercial complex nutrient is BD-Difco TC Yeastolate before the separate recipe processing steps. JCM896 explicitly names TC Yeastolate (BD-Difco) as a weighed ingredient; its catalogue and lot are unstated. The two TOGO2179/2578-derived recipe occurrences explicitly identify BD255772 in 10% and 2% preparations. The primary paper Characterization of yeastolate fractions that promote insect cell growth and recombinant protein production (PMC2267510), methods section Yeastolate and preparation of yeastolate fractions, independently identifies Difco TC yeastolate catalogue255772 purchased from Becton Dickinson, then describes dissolving and ultrafiltering it. The latter ultrafiltration and ethanol fractions are subsequent preparations and are not intrinsic properties assigned to the product here. The common TC product name and manufacturer support this bounded product-family identity; a particular catalogue or lot is not retroactively assigned to JCM896. Raw labels TC Yeastolate (BD-Difco) and TC Yeastolate (BD 255772) are retained as occurrence provenance without global synonym approval. Do not merge this product with generic yeast extract, historical Proteose Yeastolate Difco5577-15, the MICRO0000522 2%-autoclaved stock, or whole 2%/10% solutions. No composition, lot invariance, catalogue-successor equivalence or individual nutrient role is asserted.",
        "kind": "new_owner",
        "integration_obligations": [
          "Preserve source holds and exact occurrence-level scope.",
          "No merger with a taxon, generic yeast extract, differently processed preparation or concentration stock.",
          "Independent skeptical review and native content-bound validation before guarded application."
        ]
      }
