          "CM_NAME:cfad1fac04ef2d227458d27da4c27cffaedc5f24df493269df098a0bf71f6faf"
        ],
        "description": "Roscoff PCR-S11 protocol2019 (DOI10.17504/protocols.io.sz3ef8n), section4, defines this Gaffron+Se stock by adding the15listed solutes to500ml water then making a final1L, refrigerated. The payload transcribes the printed mg/L column, not recalculated rounded micromolar values. Actual PDF pages4–5 confirm cadmium nitrate Cd(NO3)2·4H2O and potassium aluminium sulfate KAl(SO4)2·12H2O; these are not guesses from TOGO malformed Cd(NO3).4H2O and KAI(SO4)2.12H2O. Raw TOGO text remains unchanged in evidence. The protocol prints5.16mg/L ammonium molybdate tetrahydrate and1.5mg/L vanadyl sulfate pentahydrate, with footnotes4.94 and1.52 respectively for the original recipe. Its receiving medium uses0.1ml/L and states this gives twice the original PCR-S11 Gaffron level. TOGO M2262 instead records0.5ml/L and a stock table roughly tenfold lower (for example H3BO3 300uM versus this protocol3008.25uM; Ni salt3uM versus30uM). These versions and inconsistent source-dose context are not collapsed. The frozen0.5G_PER_L is also a volume/unit error. This concrete2019stock is a version-qualified related preparation proposal, not automatic identity or composition assignment to the frozen M2262 occurrence. Raw Trace metals Gaffron+Se is not a global alias. All child references remain UNMAPPED, and no complete-medium release is implied. Protocol section6 states that added nutrients have been autoclaved except vitamins; the listed Gaffron+Se nutrient stock is therefore autoclaved before receiving-medium addition. No temperature or duration is supplied or invented.",
        "evidence_ids": [
          "C-E-126-SOURCE-1",
          "C-E-togo-M2262",
          "C-E-ROSCOFF-2019-PDF",
          "C-E-ROSCOFF-2019-TEXT",
          "C-E-ROSCOFF-2019-P4",
          "C-E-ROSCOFF-2019-P5",
          "C-E-ROSCOFF-2019-A-REUSE"
        ],
