        "identity_predicate_consequences": "Preserve distinct form; own-identifier exactMatch. Existing parent mappings retain their direction. New registry-only preparation has no asserted chemical equivalence.",
        "publication_review_obligation": "Coordinator must apply via guarded writers, withdraw inherited support for every changed owner byte, synchronize native exports, re-review full published payload and preserve all WITHHOLD/REJECTED gates. This proposal is not applied or approved for release.",
        "cross_shard_conflict": "Source-qualified formulation; compare other workers and existing generic owners before minting to avoid duplicate identity.",
        "limitations": "The primary JCM 900 and JCM 979 stock subrecipes specify the same nine named inputs, quantities, Metals 44 reference to JCM 149 and preparation: dissolve NTA, adjust to pH 7.0 with about 7.3 g KOH, add the remaining ingredients, and readjust to pH 6.8 with NaOH or H2SO4. Parent media and vitamin supplements differ outside this stock boundary. The literal malformed (NH4)6MoO24·4H2O remains unresolved; no heptamolybdate correction or exact chemical-component equivalence is asserted. Raw source names Hutner's basal salts (see below) and Modified Hutner's basal salts remain in the frozen case evidence; neither becomes a global stock synonym. The canonical proposed local registry identifier retains JCM 900 provenance and also covers this verified JCM 979 subrecipe. Issue1237 MIN-F02: Comparison with DSM590/1144 remains unresolved at complete chemical/preparation scope. JCM149 Metals44 prints EDTA·2Na and MnSO4·xH2O; DSM prints Na-EDTA and MnSO4·H2O plus a few drops of concentrated H2SO4. Unspecified hydration, salt detail or an unreported acid step does not prove incompatibility or equivalence. The historical malformed molybdate strings remain literal unresolved assertions. Positively different JCM149 outer Hutner mineral base has MgSO4·7H2O 14.45 g versus 29.7 g in JCM900/979; that outer recipe is distinct from the nested Metals44 reference. JCM631 also retains its positively different Mg/Ca quantities and vitamin inputs. All present immediate inputs remain unchanged; COMPLETE is source-list completeness, not resolved molecular identity.",
        "author_proposal_ids": [
          "A-PROPOSAL-JCM979_Hutner_Basal_Salts",
          "B-PROPOSAL-jcm_900_modified_hutner_basal_salts"
        ],
