        "description": "ATCC 1340 NaOH reagent (4 g/100 ml): ATCC 1340 explicitly defines its N NaOH input as 4 g/100 ml and uses 30 ml in cysteine-sulfide reducing agent. The initial reagent solvent is not specified. This explicit mass/volume definition is confined to CultureMech:009208; the five other bare-N occurrences are not automatically assigned this strength.",
        "kind": "new_owner",
        "identity_predicate_alias_consequences": "New source-qualified registry identity; no exact/broad mapping to its solute, no global raw source alias and no automatic whole-case resolution. Typed components describe only asserted parts.",
        "publication_review_obligations": "Independent source/payload review and coordinator duplicate/preparation comparison required. All source-specific holds remain. Native schema/partonomy and full-owner review must precede maintained integration.",
        "cross_shard_conflict": "Worker03 commit 1196d5bc3aaba7563b829d5cbe7e54722fccc35d proposes naoh_1m_stock/naoh_01m_stock/naoh_10m_stock. These are potential same-owner/preparation conflicts. Do not infer whole-stock equivalence solely from NaOH acid-base N/M numerical equality: carrier and source preparation remain unspecified. Before any minting, coordinator must compare precise source assertions and consolidate if actual same preparation is established; no worker03 payload or case is approved here.",
        "applicability": "Only CultureMech:009208 ingredients/18 in this six-occurrence lexical case; remaining occurrences retain unresolved numeric strength. The direct anchor remains the ATCC 1340 reagent explicitly specified as 4 g NaOH per 100 ml. For NaOH acid-base neutralization this nominal strength is consistent with 1 N; it does not establish identical carrier or full preparation. Chopped-meat protocol occurrences using 1 N are conditional comparisons only. Matching receiving meat recipes establish shared use context, not a distinct NaOH substance. The other bare-N occurrences remain unassigned.",
        "conditional_source_reconciliation": "The direct anchor remains the ATCC 1340 reagent explicitly specified as 4 g NaOH per 100 ml. For NaOH acid-base neutralization this nominal strength is consistent with 1 N; it does not establish identical carrier or full preparation. Chopped-meat protocol occurrences using 1 N are conditional comparisons only. Matching receiving meat recipes establish shared use context, not a distinct NaOH substance. The other bare-N occurrences remain unassigned.",
        "withdrawn_competing_proposal": "if1201-new-chopped_meat_1n_naoh"
      }
    },
