        "description": "Create a source-qualified preparation identity with source-named components with unknown list completeness. JCM 770 trace-element solution uses 1 mL of 32% HCl. The acid reagent has a nominal source strength and is not identical to its receiving aqueous trace-element mixture or the pure HCl owner. Literal 25%, 32% and 35% are retained as source specifications, not normalized comparable fractions. The cited sources do not state a common percentage basis, carrier, grade or assay tolerance; the exact same-or-distinct preparation relation is unresolved. TOGO M2305/M2746 explicitly calls its 25% input concentrated, so that qualitative label does not exclude a numerical percentage. If comparable definitions and assay ranges were established, a real strength difference could be assessed; they are not established here. Before co-installing overlapping candidates, the coordinator must choose an explicit common bounded partial-material scope preserving every source context, or obtain comparable preparation/product evidence. No owner merge or arbitrary winner is selected.",
